      "content": "You can argue that colonial powers introduced essential modern infrastructure, such as railways and communication networks, which were vital for integrating disparate regions into national economies. Furthermore, the imposition of standardized bureaucratic and legal systems established a framework for modern governance and commerce within these nations. These institutions, while serving colonial needs, ultimately provided the foundational structures upon which independent states could build modern administrative capacity. Therefore, this early infrastructural and legal scaffolding was a necessary precursor to contemporary statehood.",
